// Book Three, Chapter 5 (session 31). The faubourg Saint-Antoine in Lent, March 1789. The young ones, the Lictor's room, the bread.
// Opens on the faubourg by day (no phase), then one night phase of three actions out of four, then a dawn that points at the spring.
// Ends with rest() and => next. Reads b1.galerius, b1.galerius_aid, b3.weapon, b3.roll, b3.severin, b3.press, b3.sugar and b3.gallery. Chapter 6 should read hunger, standing and secrecy as this chapter left them.
@chapter b3c05
@title The Faubourg Saint-Antoine
@book crown-of-ashes
@version 1

# start
## Lent
$ b3.cadets = "heard"
$ b3.list = "unseen"
$ b3.galerius = "own"
$ b3.grain = "ignored"
$ b3.aubry = "left"
~> faubourg
